  "problem": "If $-4=-\\frac{2a}{5}$, then $a=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2a}{5}=-4\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the equation by the reciprocal of $-\\frac{2}{5},$ which is \n\n$$\n{(-\\frac{2}{5})}^{-1}=-\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2a}{5} & =-4 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{2a}{5}) & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\ 1a & =\\frac{20}{2} \\\\ a & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$",
